      "side": 1,
      "message": "But wait, what about this situation:\n\n1. base_pwr_fault_interrupt --\u003e power disable, deferred call\n2. check_and_reapply_base_power_deferred --\u003e power enable, attempts \u003d 1, deferred call for clear_base_power_on_attempts_deferred\n3. base_pwr_fault_interrupt within 1 second --\u003e power disable, deferred call\n4. check_and_reapply_base_power_deferred --\u003e power enable, attempts \u003d 2, deferred call for clear_base_power_on_attempts_deferred\n5. base_pwr_fault_interrupt within 1 second --\u003e power disable, deferred call\n6. check_and_reapply_base_power_deferred --\u003e power enable, attempts \u003d 3, deferred call for clear_base_power_on_attempts_deferred\n7. base_pwr_fault_interrupt within 1 second --\u003e power disable, deferred call\n8. check_and_reapply_base_power_deferred --\u003e attempts reached. nothing to do.\n9. after 1 second, clear_base_power_on_attempts_deferred clears attempts\u003d0.\n\nNow either:\n1. Base would recover --\u003e which you mentioned that the intention is user should disconnect and reconnect the base.\n\n2. fault still triggers --\u003e this code would still enable power to base and set attempts to 1. Shouldn\u0027t you at least disable fault interrupt at step #8?",
